ers–Kronig transform of ε₂","aside":"PyStratify evaluates each model's ε₁ in closed form. The reference rebuilds it from ε₂ alone,\n\n$$\\varepsilon_1(E) = \\varepsilon_\\infty + \\frac{2}{\\pi}\\,\\mathrm{P}\\!\\int_0^\\infty \\frac{E'\\,\\varepsilon_2(E')}{E'^2 - E^2}\\,dE'$$\n\nby QUADPACK with a Cauchy weight, split at the kinks, independent of PyStratify's own transform.\n\nTauc–Lorentz: $A$ = 120 eV, $E_0$ = 3.6 eV, $C$ = 2.4 eV, $E_g$ = 1.6 eV, at every energy. Cody–Lorentz: the same with $E_p$ = 0.8 eV, $E_t$ = 1.8 eV, $E_u$ = 0.05 eV, at every fourth."}
